#: sdlc/processes/bean-close.bpmn:76
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "`status: scrapped`, plus a \"Reasons for Scrapping\" section. This is what \"disable\" means here — the CLI has no disabled state; its vocabulary is draft, todo, in-progress, completed, scrapped. The agent's own `beans update`; the engine has no scrap op. DELETION IS NEVER THE ANSWER, even though `beans delete` exists. A scrapped bean records that the work was considered and rejected, and why; a deleted one leaves a sibling session unable to tell abandonment from accident, and leaves the next agent free to re-open the same dead end."
msgstr ""

