#: sdlc/processes/bean-close.bpmn:97
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Blocked is not scrapped. Set `--blocked-by`, say in the body what would unblock it, and return it to `todo` so it is visible to whoever can act. An in-progress bean nobody is progressing reads as active work. Not archived: the work is still wanted."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/bean-close.bpmn:35
#. Diagram label
msgid "Close the bean"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/bean-close.bpmn:45
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Closes only the bean its caller opened and claimed — Process_BeanOpen already sent someone else's to its sibling — and picks one of three recorded endings for it."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/bean-close.bpmn:63
#. Diagram label
msgid "Complete (no unchecked todos left)"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/bean-close.bpmn:111
#. Diagram label
msgid "done"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/bean-close.bpmn:89
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Move the bean, now completed or scrapped, into the archive, with a line saying which process closed it. A bean still open stays where it is with a note saying why: only a completed or scrapped bean may be archived (check:bean-archive), and only once the calling process has finished. The periodic sweep (`beans archive`) still archives anything this step leaves — it stays the floor, this op the exception (`todo-manager` § Archiving). The owner's 2026-10-20 ruling keeps archive a per-activity op; this is that activity, shared by both terminal outcomes and by every caller."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/bean-close.bpmn:112
#. Diagram label
msgid "not wanted"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/bean-close.bpmn:64
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Only once nothing is unchecked, and with a summary of what changed. The engine's `resolve` completes a bean only after the instance itself has completed, or has nothing left but archive steps — whether work is done is a judgement, and a bean is not closed on someone else's say-so. The only `resolve` op in the corpus (`check:bean-calls`)."
msgstr ""

