msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/bean-close.bpmn:57
#. Diagram label
msgid "The caller's work has stopped"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/bean-close.bpmn:36
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The closing half of every bean's life: end it in a state that says why. Done work is completed and archived; unwanted work is scrapped with its reasons — never deleted — and archived; blocked work records what it waits on and goes back to `todo` for whoever can act. Called, never run on its own, straight before an end event of a process that called Process_BeanOpen. A bean is never deleted. A scrapped bean stops the next agent re-entering a dead end; a deleted one leaves a sibling unable to tell abandonment from accident."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/bean-close.bpmn:60
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The performer's judgement on the work the caller did, and one of three recorded endings. `done`: complete it only when no todo is unchecked, with a summary of what changed. `not wanted`: set it `scrapped` with a 'Reasons for Scrapping' section — never delete. `blocked`: record what it waits on with `--blocked-by`, say what would unblock it, and return it to `todo`, because an in-progress bean nobody is progressing reads as active work. The caller's end event usually says which: an end named for success is `done`, one named for a refusal or a decline is `not wanted`, one named for an undetermined answer is `blocked`."
msgstr ""
